You are tasked with creating a new JavaFX application to manage the
HorrorCharacter objects you created in a previous assignment.
The program should have the following features:

          -CRUD functionality (Create, Read, Update, Delete).
        The “Read” portion can come from a fake backend that simply populates a structure with HorrorCharacters,
        in a manner of your choosing.

            -Two scenes, each with an FXML view, and a Controller
            The ability to pass data between the two Scenes, via the usage of a AppState class

-GUI Features:

            -TextFields, labels, and buttons

        -A ListView (bonus points if it is editable and linked to the backend)

            -RadioButtons or a ComboBox – used to select the subtype of HorrorCharacter to create

        -A DatePicker  - Add a field to base class HorrorCharacter that stores a LocalDate.
        This can represent anything of your choosing, such as a “DateOfRebirth” or “lastAttacked”.

        -Two other JavaFX GUI features that were not covered in class or in the text.

        -An interface that doesn’t look like hot garbage.